        "title": "Debug and Toolchain - JTAG/SWD, Cross-Compilation, HAL, Testing, OTA",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The embedded development loop is fundamentally split across two machines: you\n*build* on a powerful host and *run* on a resource-starved target, with a\nhardware debug probe bridging them. There's no terminal on the MCU, no `gdb`\nrunning locally, no package manager on the device. Everything — compiling,\nflashing, debugging, testing, and field updates — is shaped by that host/target\nsplit. This file is the production reality that decides whether firmware ships."
    }
